WEBVTT

00:30:28.329 --> 00:30:30.234
and one of his colleagues had an idea.

00:30:30.258 --> 00:30:31.932
RS: He says, "Well, tell you what,

00:30:31.956 --> 00:30:33.861
why don't we bring them in all at once?

00:30:33.885 --> 00:30:36.623
If we can get 50 people,
let's bring them in all at once."

00:30:36.647 --> 00:30:38.773
And we changed it into an audition.

00:30:38.797 --> 00:30:41.957
So we don't ask questions
and we don't look at resumes.

00:30:41.981 --> 00:30:45.004
AG: I'm sorry, did you say
you don't even look at their resumes?

00:30:45.028 --> 00:30:49.170
RS: So we look at them to filter,
sort of, what role they're looking for,

00:30:49.194 --> 00:30:51.211
but the people who are doing the interview

00:30:51.235 --> 00:30:54.316
have no access to the resumes
of the people we're interviewing.

00:30:54.340 --> 00:30:56.356
AG: And you don't worry that you're losing

00:30:56.380 --> 00:30:58.190
valuable information that way?

00:30:58.214 --> 00:31:01.250
RS: Well, we're worried
we're going to lose valuable information